Prerequisites
Python 3.10+ installed on Windows
Microsoft Edge browser (Selenium uses Edge by default)
PowerShell for running API client commands
Internet connection for Banner access

Installation
1. clone repository or download as zip file
cd autoadvisor-dev

Running API server (In the First Terminal)
cd C:\path\to\autoadvisor-dev
python Main.py

You should see 
[INFO] AutoAdvisor API listening on http://localhost:8001

Open a second terminal and run this fetch transcript script
$req = @{
    username    = 'your-vsu-email@students.vsu.edu'
    password    = 'your-banner-password'
    advisor     = 'Wang'  # or your advisor's name
} | ConvertTo-Json

$response = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri http://localhost:8001/api/fetch-transcript `
                              -Method POST -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $req

$sessionId = $response.session_id

$pinReq = @{
    session_id = $sessionId  # from step 2
    pin        = '1234'      # replace with actual PIN from Okta
} | ConvertTo-Json

$transcript = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri http://localhost:8001/api/submit-pin `
                                -Method POST -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $pinReq

$transcript

What happens:

Browser opens and navigates to Banner login
Enter your credentials manually in the browser
Okta sends a PIN to your authenticator app
Submit the PIN via the API call above
Selenium scrapes your transcript and organizes courses by semester
Transcript data is printed to the first terminal and returned in the response
Final Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "session_id": "session_1772124886.747894",
  "transcript_data": {
    "name": "Your Name",
    "v_number": "VXXXXXXX",
    "advisor": "Wang",
    "semesters": [
      {
        "label": "Freshman 1",
        "description": "FALL 2022",
        "courses": [...]
      },
      ...
    ]
  },
  "message": "Transcript fetched successfully"
}

API Endpoints
POST /api/fetch-transcript - Create session with credentials
POST /api/submit-pin - Submit PIN and get transcript
GET /api/session/{session_id} - Check session status
GET /api/active-sessions - List all active sessions
DELETE /api/session/{session_id} - Delete a session

